    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3dcec4b5_e1f3e9db",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2183,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076971
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-22T16:10:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By the same token, should we also not mention KeyMaster/KeyMint (\"KM\" in the following) where the Android Attestation Extension is documented? I\u0027m not trying to be facetious but... all we\u0027re saying in this CL - basically - is that the version number which can be retrieved from FEATURE_HARDWARE_KEYSTORE is the same version number which you get from Android Attestation Extension.\n\nWe have to say _something_ about what version number in FEATURE_HARDWARE_KEYSTORE is. I\u0027m open for suggestions but I don\u0027t think inventing a new \"keystore feature version number\" is going to help b/c it would just 100% correlate to KM versions anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "caf2dc5d_2500dfe6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2183,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2183,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "b4c74c256ba3736f7b267ef411b9a5788cf11eae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ceeb245_e229f361",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2183,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043663
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-23T19:40:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not the same version number you get from the attestation extension, unfortunately.\n\nMy suggestion is just that instead of saying \"This is KM version X\" (which doesn\u0027t mean anything to developers -- it means something to OEMs but not to devs) we should instead specify features. For example (each version only lists features added in that version):\n\n100 -- Hardware support for ECDH and support for app-generated attestation keys.\n41 -- Hardware enforcement of device-unlocked keys.\n40 -- Support for wrapped key import\n\nNote that there\u0027s a lot more in each version, but we would only want to reflect the app-visible features.",
      "parentUuid": "3dcec4b5_e1f3e9db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2183,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2183,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "b4c74c256ba3736f7b267ef411b9a5788cf11eae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
